  "body": "What changed:\n- `cargo xtask gate release` now plans the heavy lanes of motion and app as one release build (`--no-run`), then one step for each test target. The targets are `lib`, `bins`, `doc` and each integration binary that can hold an `#[ignore]`d test.\n- Step names are `app heavy: <binary>` and `motion heavy: <binary>`. `--only \"app heavy: pocket3d_hsm\"` runs that binary alone. `--failed` picks failed steps by their log stem.\n- The log note of a step now names the failed tests (`[tests: ...]`) and each test that libtest reports as running over N seconds (`slow: ...`).\n- AGENTS.md \"Three gate tiers\" describes the steps. The decision file is `docs/decisions/1714-heavy-lane-steps.md`.\n- The dry run lists 151 heavy steps instead of 2. No test in `crates/` is changed, removed or un-ignored.\n\nPinning tests (xtask unit tests):\n- `heavy_tests::heavy_lanes_are_one_build_then_one_step_per_target`\n- `heavy_tests::heavy_steps_skip_only_binaries_without_ignored_tests`: every binary with an `#[ignore]` in any file has a step, so the set of tests does not drop.\n- `heavy_tests::heavy_only_selects_one_binary_and_the_failed_log_picks_it_back`\n- `heavy_tests::log_note_names_failed_tests_and_slow_tests`\n- `tests::batch_skips_slow_binaries_and_release_runs_everything` (updated plan shape)\n\nNot exercised:\n- The release tier did not run. Only `--dry-run` and the xtask unit tests ran (131 pass, clippy clean).\n- Kernel heavy steps are not added. The release tier never ran kernel `--ignored` before. This is a coverage change.\n  Follow-up: #1783.\n- A time limit for a heavy test needs nightly `--report-time`. The note lists the slow tests that libtest reports.\n\nProcess change: yes\nChangelog: none\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #1714\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
